{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407247-abomination-shapeshifting-description","id":407247,"title":"Abomination shapeshifting description?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T19:05:18-08:00","id":407247,"title":"Abomination shapeshifting description?","content":"Some of you may have seen the thread I started some time ago where I asked if the ritual of sacred rebirth would work on an embraced kinfolk. Well, I kind of disregarded what was said there in favor of actually allowing said ritual to work, which you might not agree with and I'm not asking you to, but I would like some feedback on how such an Abomination's shapeshifting would look like.<br /> <br /> The Abomination is going to be a Get of Fenris kinfolk turned Lasombra Antitribu. I'm thinking shapeshifting may be something obtenebration influenced, like having the Abomination melt into a pool of shadow and then claw it's way out of it in whatever form it changed into.<br /> <br /> If you have any ideas I'd love to hear them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:29:41-08:00","id":407279,"title":"","content":"perhaps have its flesh drip and melt away in patches of viscous shadow stuffs..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5056-zerd","name":"Zerd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:55:15-08:00","id":407289,"title":"","content":"Abominations are detailed in the wild west companion for werewolf. I believe they shapeshift same as any other werewolf. The thing that looks mutated apparently is the fangs. The thing about the curse is they lose permanent gnosis, and eventually self destruct and can no longer step sideways. The spirits will no longer talk with them, they can no longer learn gifts in the normal ways, only from banes. Banes follow them and destroy everything around them. They're lonely monsters that even black spirals loath. Such an abomination to the world are the Cascara.<br /> <br /> They are however completely functional as vampires from what i understand of it. You can of course house rule it however you want and make a monster shapeshifting beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":1939,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","user":"Lyrics Of War","date":". 02-15-2015, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T09:00:26-08:00","id":407816,"title":"","content":"Garou shapeshift pretty damn fast. All the melting and clawing seems like it would take awhile. Or it would if it was going to look cool. Otherwise it would go something like: Guy turns black and instantly melts into a puddle with a BLOOP! noise, then POP! a werewolf shoots up out of the puddle. All in a couple of seconds. Unless you are going for a penalty to being an Abomination by lengthening the time it takes to change or he's getting some cool benefit from taking so long (and being hideously vulnerable during it... what if someone comes up with laddle and stirs the black goo? Or beats on the werewolf as it's trying to emerge? I'm being over the top on the comedy side here, but it is worth thinking about whether something meant to be ultra-cool might not come across that way...)<br /> <br /> Kinda like Zerd was saying, melting instantly into a black wispy shadow-self and having that heave and shift and rip away in dissolving tatters with whatever shape he's taken being revealed (with a charnel smell) might work better. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T15:44:24-08:00","id":408264,"title":"","content":"That sounds good, I was thinking of making this specific Abomination less penalty-riddled than the &quot;normal&quot; kind because of the fact that he was a vampire before he was Garou.<br /> <br /> I plan to have him be connected to the abyss in the way normal Garou are connected to Gaia and the moon. Thus he won't be harmed by silver and such but strong and concentrated light will force him into his breed form and his very presence will allow the abyss to sort of seep into the world of the living, I haven't yet decided what that might mean for his surroundings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4003-kristviljan","name":"Kristviljan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4003_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T18:44:31-08:00","id":408444,"title":"","content":"...Have you ever seen the movie &quot;The Fly&quot; by Croenemberg?. imagine it with more cancer and tumours. Add a little bit of The Thing into the Mix and youre Go...oh, and add a lot of eldtrich screamings of something trying to say (in a very low and distorted way) the words &quot;Kill Me.&quot;, id magine that each transformation was incredibly brutal and different from each other since its..well..AN ABOMINATION AGAINST NATURE!<br /> <br /> Seeing it should always comes to mind the Phrase &quot;KILL IT WITH FIRE BEFORE IT CAN REPRODUCE!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}